{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Borrow the inspection context shared by this criterion's operations.\n    pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>;\n}\n```\n\n`ValidationContext::inspection()` exposes the execution's `InspectionContext`.\nThe SDK's supplied agent uses that same context for graph-node reads,\noutgoing-edge queries, and delivery recording. The application supplies data\nthrough its domain; the SDK supplies and dispatches the tools.\n\nBorrowing the context does not record an input. The reads and edge selections\nperformed through it contribute the observations described below.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations of `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.shared_context` are met.\n\n**Signature.** `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[inspection]` is `pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>`. It sits in `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>`. It returns `&self.inspection`, a borrow of the execution's own context. The `ValidationContext` struct holds that field as `inspection: InspectionContext<'d, D>`, set in `configured`. Because the method only borrows, it records no input.\n\n**The supplied agent uses the same context.**\n- `procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` calls `agent.run(request, &self.ctx.inspection)`. It passes the very context that `inspection()` exposes.\n- The `Agent::run` trait method takes `inspection: &'a InspectionContext<'_, D>`.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` stores that reference in `GraphSession`. The struct `GraphSession` holds `inspection: &'a InspectionContext<'d, D>`. The code does not create a second context.\n- `tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` performs graph-node reads with `self.inspection.prepare_read`. It performs outgoing-edge queries with `self.inspection.prepare_edges`. Both go through the shared context.\n- `tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[delivered]` records delivery. It calls `self.inspection.observe_read` and `self.inspection.observe_edges` on the same context.\n- The SDK supplies and dispatches the tools: `dispatch` matches `read_node`, `get_node_page` and `outgoing_edges`. Any other tool name goes to the application-supplied `self.tools` session. The application's domain supplies the data.\n\nBorrowing the context records nothing. Observations are recorded only in `delivered` and in `execute`'s `observe_edges_by`, which come from the reads and edge selections themselves.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. No FIXME acknowledgments apply. This is a structural check only. The text names no obligation that depends on a test.",
